# App platform — Terraform

## Layout

- AWS site module under `infra/terraform/aws/modules/…`
- Env roots: `infra/terraform/aws/envs/stg`, `envs/prod`
- Shared state bootstrap: `infra/terraform/aws/bootstrap`
- Cloudflare + Grafana: separate roots, same S3 backend

## Naming

Prefer `[environment]-[app]-[purpose]-[resource-type]` (and `shared-[app]-…` for account-wide). Derive from `var.environment` / app slug in locals — do not scatter hard-coded legacy names.

## State

- Remote state + S3 native locking (`use_lockfile = true`; Terraform >= 1.10).
- Separate keys per root (`bootstrap/`, `envs/stg/`, `envs/prod/`, `cloudflare/`, `grafana/`, …).
- Never commit `*.tfstate` or `terraform.tfvars`.
- Backends do not pin `profile=`; locally `export AWS_PROFILE=7oas7er`.

## CI

- Plan-only workflow (fmt / validate / Checkov / plan) — **not** apply. See `docs/adr/0003-local-terraform-apply.md`.
- Path-filter so unchanged roots skip validate/plan.

## Regions / IAM habits

- Regional default `eu-north-1` (`app-aws-regions`); ACM for CloudFront aliases in `us-east-1`.
- IAM: `aws_iam_policy_document` in `data.tf`, not inline JSON on the policy resource.
- Cloudflare-only origin gate belongs in the site module; rotate secrets per `SECURITY.md` / origin-verify runbook when used.
